window.UNIT5_DATA={"sections":[["warm-up","Warm Up","Start with your experience of orders; read and discuss the opening story."],["part-01-vocabulary","Part 1 · Vocabulary and Terminology","Orders, order details, documents, and useful word combinations."],["part-02-grammar","Part 2 · Grammar","Present simple, sequence words, and imperatives."],["part-03-listening","Part 3 · Listening and Dialogue","Listen to Ms. Chen, Fadi, and Karim handle an order."],["part-04-speaking","Part 4 · Speaking and Your Role","Practise placing, checking, and confirming an order."],["part-05-reading","Part 5 · Extended Reading","The one wrong number: why careful checking matters."],["part-06-writing","Part 6 · Writing","Write a clear order-confirmation email."],["part-07-trade-skills","Part 7 · Trade-Skills Track","Read a purchase order and check its details."],["part-08-consolidation","Part 8 · Consolidation","Follow Fadi as he catches a delivery-address mistake."],["part-09-cases","Part 9 · Case Studies and Decisions","Choose safe actions for three order-handling cases."],["part-10-review","Part 10 · Review and Can-Do","Review vocabulary, grammar, reading, listening, speaking, and writing."],["part-11-foundations","Part 11 · Foundations for Further Study","Reflect on care, accuracy, and trust at work."]],"pages":{"warm-up":{"title":"Warm Up · Orders and careful checking","intro":"Think about the documents and checking steps used in your own work.","exercises":[{"type":"writing","prompt":"When someone buys from your company, what document do they send?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"Why is it important to check every detail in an order?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"How do you say the steps of a job in order? Try First…, Then…","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"What does Ms. Chen send to place an order?","options":["An invoice","A purchase order (PO)","A delivery note","A quotation"],"answer":"A purchase order (PO)","explain":"A purchase order tells the seller what the customer wants to buy.","feedback":["Not quite: “An invoice” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “A purchase order (PO)”. A purchase order tells the seller what the customer wants to buy.","Correct. A purchase order tells the seller what the customer wants to buy.","Not quite: “A delivery note” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “A purchase order (PO)”. A purchase order tells the seller what the customer wants to buy.","Not quite: “A quotation” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “A purchase order (PO)”. A purchase order tells the seller what the customer wants to buy."]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"A. Comprehension: What is Fadi’s job with the order? Name three order details. What steps does he follow? What mistake does he find and what does he do? What does his confirmation email say?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"B1. Fadi checks every detail carefully.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explain":"Fadi checks each detail carefully.","feedback":["Correct. Fadi checks each detail carefully.","Not quite. The statement is true. Fadi checks each detail carefully."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"B2. The product is cement.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explain":"The order is for cement.","feedback":["Correct. The order is for cement.","Not quite. The statement is true. The order is for cement."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"B3. The reference number is correct on the first PO.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explain":"The first PO says PO-1234; the correct number is PO-1243.","feedback":["Not quite. The statement is false. The first PO says PO-1234; the correct number is PO-1243.","Correct. The first PO says PO-1234; the correct number is PO-1243."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"B4. Fadi ignores the mistake.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explain":"Fadi writes to Ms. Chen and asks her to check it.","feedback":["Not quite. The statement is false. Fadi writes to Ms. Chen and asks her to check it.","Correct. Fadi writes to Ms. Chen and asks her to check it."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"B5. Ms. Chen corrects the reference number.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explain":"Ms. Chen replies and corrects it.","feedback":["Correct. Ms. Chen replies and corrects it.","Not quite. The statement is true. Ms. Chen replies and corrects it."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"B6. The order is approved.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explain":"Fadi’s confirmation says the order is approved.","feedback":["Correct. Fadi’s confirmation says the order is approved.","Not quite. The statement is true. Fadi’s confirmation says the order is approved."]},{"type":"match","prompt":"C. Find the words in the story that match these meanings.","pairs":[["say “yes, we have your order”","confirm"],["the number that names an order","reference number"],["the person or company who buys","customer"],["right; with no mistake","correct"]]},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"Answer from the opening story.","items":[["A holding group has many smaller companies ____.","inside it"],["The Group works in ____ sectors.","six"],["Karim is the Financial ____.","Controller"],["NorthBridge wants to buy cement and ____.","iron"]]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"True or false: Ms. Chen is from NorthBridge.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explain":"The story introduces Ms. Chen as a partner from NorthBridge Industrial Trading.","feedback":["Correct. The story introduces Ms. Chen as a partner from NorthBridge Industrial Trading.","Not quite. The statement is true. The story introduces Ms. Chen as a partner from NorthBridge Industrial Trading."]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"D. Over to you: How do you check an order at your company? What do you do if you find a mistake? How do you confirm an order to a customer?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."}],"reading":"Ms. Chen likes the quotation. Now she places an ORDER. She sends a document called a PURCHASE ORDER, or “PO” for short. A purchase order says: “I want to buy this. This is the quantity. This is the price. This is my company.”\n\nFadi, the Administrative Assistant, receives the purchase order. His job is to check it, confirm it, and record it. An order has many details—the product, quantity, price, customer’s name, and reference number. If one detail is wrong, there is a problem. So Fadi checks every detail carefully.\n\n“Let me check the order,” says Fadi. “First, I read the purchase order. Then I check the details. The product is cement—correct. The quantity is 1,000 tonnes—correct. The price is 45 dollars per tonne—correct.” But then Fadi sees a small mistake. “Wait,” he says. “The reference number is wrong. The PO says PO-1234, but our number is PO-1243.” Fadi does not ignore the mistake. He writes to Ms. Chen: “Dear Ms. Chen, thank you for your order. There is a small mistake in the reference number. Please can you check it? Best, Fadi.” Ms. Chen replies quickly and corrects it.\n\nNow the order is correct. Fadi confirms it. He writes an order-confirmation email: “Dear Ms. Chen, thank you for your order. We confirm: cement, 1,000 tonnes, 45 dollars per tonne, total 45,000 dollars. Reference: PO-1243. Your order is approved. Best regards, Fadi.”\n\n“A good confirmation,” says Karim. “Now Ms. Chen knows we have her order, and that all the details are correct. This is how we work: receive, check, confirm. Every order, the same way. When you check carefully and confirm clearly, there are no problems later.” And so, we place the order, check it, and confirm it—a big step towards the delivery.","scene":"Office"},"part-01-vocabulary":{"title":"Part 1 · Vocabulary and Terminology","intro":"Orders and documents: learn the words, inspect an order, and practise common word partnerships.","exercises":[{"type":"match","prompt":"A. Match each word to its meaning. One meaning is extra.","pairs":[["order","a request to buy products"],["purchase order","the document a customer sends to buy"],["confirm","to say “yes, we have your order”"],["reference number","the number that names an order"],["customer","the person or company who buys"],["approved","accepted; agreed"],["correct","right; with no mistake"],["details","the small pieces of information"]]},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"B. Complete with the word bank: order · purchase order · confirm · reference number · customer · details.","items":[["Ms. Chen places an ____ for 1,000 tonnes.","order"],["She sends a ____ (PO) with all the information.","purchase order"],["Fadi checks the ____: product, quantity, and price.","details"],["The ____ is PO-1243.","reference number"],["The ____ is NorthBridge.","customer"],["Fadi writes to ____ the order.","confirm"]]},{"type":"match","prompt":"C. Match the PO field to the order detail.","pairs":[["Product","cement"],["Quantity","1,000 tonnes"],["Reference number","PO-1243"],["Customer","NorthBridge"]]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Which item is the product in this order?","options":["purchase order","confirmation","cement","reference number"],"answer":"cement","explain":"Cement is the product being bought. A purchase order and confirmation are documents, and the reference number identifies the order.","feedback":["Not quite: “purchase order” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “cement”. Cement is the product being bought. A purchase order and confirmation are documents, and the reference number identifies the order.","Not quite: “confirmation” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “cement”. Cement is the product being bought. A purchase order and confirmation are documents, and the reference number identifies the order.","Correct. Cement is the product being bought. A purchase order and confirmation are documents, and the reference number identifies the order.","Not quite: “reference number” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “cement”. Cement is the product being bought. A purchase order and confirmation are documents, and the reference number identifies the order."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Which word means accepted or officially agreed?","options":["approved","quantity","reference","tonnes"],"answer":"approved","explain":"Approved describes an order that has been accepted. Quantity and tonnes describe how much; a reference identifies the order.","feedback":["Correct. Approved describes an order that has been accepted. Quantity and tonnes describe how much; a reference identifies the order.","Not quite: “quantity” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “approved”. Approved describes an order that has been accepted. Quantity and tonnes describe how much; a reference identifies the order.","Not quite: “reference” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “approved”. Approved describes an order that has been accepted. Quantity and tonnes describe how much; a reference identifies the order.","Not quite: “tonnes” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “approved”. Approved describes an order that has been accepted. Quantity and tonnes describe how much; a reference identifies the order."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Which word means the person or company buying the goods?","options":["customer","supplier","carrier","accountant"],"answer":"customer","explain":"The customer buys the goods. A supplier sells them, a carrier transports them, and an accountant handles financial records.","feedback":["Correct. The customer buys the goods. A supplier sells them, a carrier transports them, and an accountant handles financial records.","Not quite: “supplier” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “customer”. The customer buys the goods. A supplier sells them, a carrier transports them, and an accountant handles financial records.","Not quite: “carrier” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “customer”. The customer buys the goods. A supplier sells them, a carrier transports them, and an accountant handles financial records.","Not quite: “accountant” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “customer”. The customer buys the goods. A supplier sells them, a carrier transports them, and an accountant handles financial records."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Which action means entering order information into company records?","options":["record","confirm","check","deliver"],"answer":"record","explain":"To record is to enter and keep the order information. To check is to inspect it; to confirm is to say it is accepted; to deliver is to transport the goods.","feedback":["Correct. To record is to enter and keep the order information. To check is to inspect it; to confirm is to say it is accepted; to deliver is to transport the goods.","Not quite: “confirm” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “record”. To record is to enter and keep the order information. To check is to inspect it; to confirm is to say it is accepted; to deliver is to transport the goods.","Not quite: “check” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “record”. To record is to enter and keep the order information. To check is to inspect it; to confirm is to say it is accepted; to deliver is to transport the goods.","Not quite: “deliver” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “record”. To record is to enter and keep the order information. To check is to inspect it; to confirm is to say it is accepted; to deliver is to transport the goods."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Which detail identifies one order among many orders?","options":["reference number","quantity","total","delivery address"],"answer":"reference number","explain":"The reference number names and separates the order. Quantity is how much is ordered, total is the final cost, and the address says where goods go.","feedback":["Correct. The reference number names and separates the order. Quantity is how much is ordered, total is the final cost, and the address says where goods go.","Not quite: “quantity” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “reference number”. The reference number names and separates the order. Quantity is how much is ordered, total is the final cost, and the address says where goods go.","Not quite: “total” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “reference number”. The reference number names and separates the order. Quantity is how much is ordered, total is the final cost, and the address says where goods go.","Not quite: “delivery address” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “reference number”. The reference number names and separates the order. Quantity is how much is ordered, total is the final cost, and the address says where goods go."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"A customer asks to buy products. What is the request called?","options":["an order","a quotation","an invoice","a delivery note"],"answer":"an order","explain":"An order is a request to buy. A quotation offers prices, an invoice requests payment, and a delivery note accompanies goods.","feedback":["Correct. An order is a request to buy. A quotation offers prices, an invoice requests payment, and a delivery note accompanies goods.","Not quite: “a quotation” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “an order”. An order is a request to buy. A quotation offers prices, an invoice requests payment, and a delivery note accompanies goods.","Not quite: “an invoice” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “an order”. An order is a request to buy. A quotation offers prices, an invoice requests payment, and a delivery note accompanies goods.","Not quite: “a delivery note” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “an order”. An order is a request to buy. A quotation offers prices, an invoice requests payment, and a delivery note accompanies goods."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"After checking an order, Fadi says, 'We ____ your order.' Which verb means 'say it is received and accepted'?","options":["confirm","receive","record","deliver"],"answer":"confirm","explain":"Confirm means to say the order is received and accepted. Receive is to get it, record is to enter its details, and deliver is to transport the goods.","feedback":["Correct. Confirm means to say the order is received and accepted. Receive is to get it, record is to enter its details, and deliver is to transport the goods.","Not quite: “receive” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “confirm”. Confirm means to say the order is received and accepted. Receive is to get it, record is to enter its details, and deliver is to transport the goods.","Not quite: “record” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “confirm”. Confirm means to say the order is received and accepted. Receive is to get it, record is to enter its details, and deliver is to transport the goods.","Not quite: “deliver” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “confirm”. Confirm means to say the order is received and accepted. Receive is to get it, record is to enter its details, and deliver is to transport the goods."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Which detail names a particular order so both sides can refer to it?","options":["reference number","invoice total","quantity","product"],"answer":"reference number","explain":"The reference number identifies a particular order. Quantity says how much; product says what is being bought; invoice total says how much money is due.","feedback":["Correct. The reference number identifies a particular order. Quantity says how much; product says what is being bought; invoice total says how much money is due.","Not quite: “invoice total” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “reference number”. The reference number identifies a particular order. Quantity says how much; product says what is being bought; invoice total says how much money is due.","Not quite: “quantity” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “reference number”. The reference number identifies a particular order. Quantity says how much; product says what is being bought; invoice total says how much money is due.","Not quite: “product” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “reference number”. The reference number identifies a particular order. Quantity says how much; product says what is being bought; invoice total says how much money is due."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"A company buys cement from another company. What is the buying company?","options":["the customer","the supplier","the carrier","the manufacturer"],"answer":"the customer","explain":"The customer is the buyer. The supplier sells the product, the carrier transports it, and the manufacturer produces it.","feedback":["Correct. The customer is the buyer. The supplier sells the product, the carrier transports it, and the manufacturer produces it.","Not quite: “the supplier” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “the customer”. The customer is the buyer. The supplier sells the product, the carrier transports it, and the manufacturer produces it.","Not quite: “the carrier” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “the customer”. The customer is the buyer. The supplier sells the product, the carrier transports it, and the manufacturer produces it.","Not quite: “the manufacturer” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “the customer”. The customer is the buyer. The supplier sells the product, the carrier transports it, and the manufacturer produces it."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"In 'The order is for 1,000 tonnes', what does 1,000 describe?","options":["the quantity","the price per tonne","the reference number","the total cost"],"answer":"the quantity","explain":"Quantity tells how much product the customer ordered. Price is the cost per unit, the reference number identifies the order, and the total cost is the full amount of money.","feedback":["Correct. Quantity tells how much product the customer ordered. Price is the cost per unit, the reference number identifies the order, and the total cost is the full amount of money.","Not quite: “the price per tonne” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “the quantity”. Quantity tells how much product the customer ordered. Price is the cost per unit, the reference number identifies the order, and the total cost is the full amount of money.","Not quite: “the reference number” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “the quantity”. Quantity tells how much product the customer ordered. Price is the cost per unit, the reference number identifies the order, and the total cost is the full amount of money.","Not quite: “the total cost” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “the quantity”. Quantity tells how much product the customer ordered. Price is the cost per unit, the reference number identifies the order, and the total cost is the full amount of money."]},{"type":"match","prompt":"F. Match the two halves.","pairs":[["place an","order"],["check the","details"],["confirm","the order"],["correct","a mistake"],["reference","number"]]},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"G. Complete the paragraph.","items":[["Fadi receives an ____ from NorthBridge.","order"],["He checks the ____.","details"],["and the ____ number.","reference"],["He makes sure everything is ____.","correct"],["Then he writes to ____ the order.","confirm"],["for the ____.","customer"]]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"H. Write a sentence using at least three order words: order, confirm, reference, customer, approved.","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."}],"reading":null,"scene":"Office"},"part-02-grammar":{"title":"Part 2 · Grammar","intro":"Describe a process with the present simple, put steps in order, and give clear instructions.","exercises":[{"type":"blanks","prompt":"A/I. Complete with the present simple.","items":[["Fadi ____ (check) the details.","checks"],["We ____ (confirm) every order.","confirm"],["The customer ____ (send) a purchase order.","sends"],["The system ____ (make) a reference number.","makes"],["We ____ (receive) the order.","receive"]]},{"type":"order","prompt":"B. Put the order-confirmation process in order.","items":["First, we receive the order.","Then we check the details.","Next, we correct any mistake.","After that, we prepare the confirmation.","Finally, we confirm the order."]},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"C. Complete with First, Then, Next, Finally.","items":[["____, we receive the order.","First"],["____, we check the details.","Then"],["____, we correct any mistake.","Next"],["____, we confirm the order.","Finally"]]},{"type":"order","prompt":"D/J. Build each instruction by arranging its words.","items":[["Check","the details."],["Confirm","the order."],["Don't forget","the number."],["Please check","the quantity."],["Don't confirm","a wrong order."]]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Fadi ____ every order before confirmation. (routine)","options":["checks","is checking","check","checked"],"answer":"checks","explain":"A routine uses the present simple. With he/Fadi, add -s: checks. 'Is checking' describes something happening now.","feedback":["Correct. A routine uses the present simple. With he/Fadi, add -s: checks. 'Is checking' describes something happening now.","Not quite: “is checking” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “checks”. A routine uses the present simple. With he/Fadi, add -s: checks. 'Is checking' describes something happening now.","Not quite: “check” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “checks”. A routine uses the present simple. With he/Fadi, add -s: checks. 'Is checking' describes something happening now.","Not quite: “checked” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “checks”. A routine uses the present simple. With he/Fadi, add -s: checks. 'Is checking' describes something happening now."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Fadi ____ this purchase order right now. (happening now)","options":["is checking","checks","check","checked"],"answer":"is checking","explain":"Right now points to the present continuous: is + verb-ing. Use 'checks' for a routine, such as 'Fadi checks every order.'","feedback":["Correct. Right now points to the present continuous: is + verb-ing. Use 'checks' for a routine, such as 'Fadi checks every order.'","Not quite: “checks” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “is checking”. Right now points to the present continuous: is + verb-ing. Use 'checks' for a routine, such as 'Fadi checks every order.'","Not quite: “check” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “is checking”. Right now points to the present continuous: is + verb-ing. Use 'checks' for a routine, such as 'Fadi checks every order.'","Not quite: “checked” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “is checking”. Right now points to the present continuous: is + verb-ing. Use 'checks' for a routine, such as 'Fadi checks every order.'"]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"____ the details, please. (polite instruction)","options":["Check","Checks","Are checking","Checked"],"answer":"Check","explain":"An instruction uses the base verb without a subject or -s: 'Check the details.' The other forms are not imperative forms here.","feedback":["Correct. An instruction uses the base verb without a subject or -s: 'Check the details.' The other forms are not imperative forms here.","Not quite: “Checks” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Check”. An instruction uses the base verb without a subject or -s: 'Check the details.' The other forms are not imperative forms here.","Not quite: “Are checking” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Check”. An instruction uses the base verb without a subject or -s: 'Check the details.' The other forms are not imperative forms here.","Not quite: “Checked” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Check”. An instruction uses the base verb without a subject or -s: 'Check the details.' The other forms are not imperative forms here."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Choose the sentence that describes a routine.","options":["Fadi checks every order each morning.","Fadi is checking this order now.","Fadi checked the order yesterday.","Check the order, please."],"answer":"Fadi checks every order each morning.","explain":"'Each morning' describes a routine, so use the present simple. 'Is checking' is happening now, 'checked' is past, and 'Check' is an instruction.","feedback":["Correct. 'Each morning' describes a routine, so use the present simple. 'Is checking' is happening now, 'checked' is past, and 'Check' is an instruction.","Not quite: “Fadi is checking this order now.” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Fadi checks every order each morning.”. 'Each morning' describes a routine, so use the present simple. 'Is checking' is happening now, 'checked' is past, and 'Check' is an instruction.","Not quite: “Fadi checked the order yesterday.” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Fadi checks every order each morning.”. 'Each morning' describes a routine, so use the present simple. 'Is checking' is happening now, 'checked' is past, and 'Check' is an instruction.","Not quite: “Check the order, please.” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Fadi checks every order each morning.”. 'Each morning' describes a routine, so use the present simple. 'Is checking' is happening now, 'checked' is past, and 'Check' is an instruction."]},{"type":"match","prompt":"F. Match each instruction to when you say it.","pairs":[["Check the details.","before you confirm"],["Correct the mistake.","when you find an error"],["Confirm the order.","after everything is correct"],["Send the confirmation.","at the end"]]},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"G. Correct the mistake in each sentence.","items":[["You ____ the details. (checks)","check"],["____ the order, please. (To confirm)","Confirm"],["____ forget the number. (Not)","Don’t"],["The system ____ a reply. (send)","sends"]]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"H. Write the steps of a job you do. Use First…, Then…, Finally… and at least one imperative.","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."}],"reading":null,"scene":"Office"},"part-03-listening":{"title":"Part 3 · Listening and Dialogue","intro":"Listen to each conversation, replay lines, adjust speed, and answer without seeing the transcript first.","exercises":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"Dialogue 1: What does Ms. Chen want to order?","options":["1,000 tonnes of iron","1,000 tonnes of cement","100 tonnes of cement","1,000 bags of cement"],"answer":"1,000 tonnes of cement","explain":"Ms. Chen places an order for 1,000 tonnes of cement.","feedback":["Not quite: “1,000 tonnes of iron” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “1,000 tonnes of cement”. Ms. Chen places an order for 1,000 tonnes of cement.","Correct. Ms. Chen places an order for 1,000 tonnes of cement.","Not quite: “100 tonnes of cement” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “1,000 tonnes of cement”. Ms. Chen places an order for 1,000 tonnes of cement.","Not quite: “1,000 bags of cement” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “1,000 tonnes of cement”. Ms. Chen places an order for 1,000 tonnes of cement."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"What does Fadi ask Ms. Chen to send?","options":["An invoice","A delivery note","The purchase order","A quotation"],"answer":"The purchase order","explain":"Fadi asks her to send the PO.","feedback":["Not quite: “An invoice” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The purchase order”. Fadi asks her to send the PO.","Not quite: “A delivery note” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The purchase order”. Fadi asks her to send the PO.","Correct. Fadi asks her to send the PO.","Not quite: “A quotation” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The purchase order”. Fadi asks her to send the PO."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"What mistake does Fadi find?","options":["The quantity is too small","The product is wrong","The reference number is wrong","The price is missing"],"answer":"The reference number is wrong","explain":"The PO says PO-1234; the correct reference is PO-1243.","feedback":["Not quite: “The quantity is too small” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The reference number is wrong”. The PO says PO-1234; the correct reference is PO-1243.","Not quite: “The product is wrong” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The reference number is wrong”. The PO says PO-1234; the correct reference is PO-1243.","Correct. The PO says PO-1234; the correct reference is PO-1243.","Not quite: “The price is missing” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The reference number is wrong”. The PO says PO-1234; the correct reference is PO-1243."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"What will Fadi do next?","options":["Ignore the mistake","Send a confirmation email","Change the product","Cancel the order"],"answer":"Send a confirmation email","explain":"After the details are corrected, Fadi will confirm the order.","feedback":["Not quite: “Ignore the mistake” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Send a confirmation email”. After the details are corrected, Fadi will confirm the order.","Correct. After the details are corrected, Fadi will confirm the order.","Not quite: “Change the product” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Send a confirmation email”. After the details are corrected, Fadi will confirm the order.","Not quite: “Cancel the order” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Send a confirmation email”. After the details are corrected, Fadi will confirm the order."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Dialogue 2: Karim asks Fadi to check the…","options":["price","reference number","product","address"],"answer":"reference number","explain":"Karim specifically asks him to check the reference number.","feedback":["Not quite: “price” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “reference number”. Karim specifically asks him to check the reference number.","Correct. Karim specifically asks him to check the reference number.","Not quite: “product” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “reference number”. Karim specifically asks him to check the reference number.","Not quite: “address” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “reference number”. Karim specifically asks him to check the reference number."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"First, Fadi ____ the customer.","options":["calls","writes to","visits","ignores"],"answer":"writes to","explain":"Fadi says, “First, I write to the customer.”","feedback":["Not quite: “calls” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “writes to”. Fadi says, “First, I write to the customer.”","Correct. Fadi says, “First, I write to the customer.”","Not quite: “visits” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “writes to”. Fadi says, “First, I write to the customer.”","Not quite: “ignores” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “writes to”. Fadi says, “First, I write to the customer.”"]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Karim says: Don’t confirm an order with a ____ number.","options":["new","wrong","big","small"],"answer":"wrong","explain":"The instruction warns against confirming with a wrong number.","feedback":["Not quite: “new” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “wrong”. The instruction warns against confirming with a wrong number.","Correct. The instruction warns against confirming with a wrong number.","Not quite: “big” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “wrong”. The instruction warns against confirming with a wrong number.","Not quite: “small” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “wrong”. The instruction warns against confirming with a wrong number."]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"Language focus: copy one sequence word, one imperative, one present-simple step, and one polite correction from the dialogues.","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."}],"reading":"Ms. Chen: Hello, Fadi. I'd like to place an order. 1,000 tonnes of cement.\nFadi: Thank you, Ms. Chen. Please send me the purchase order.\nMs. Chen: I sent it this morning. The reference is PO-1234.\nFadi: Let me check. First, I read the PO. Then I check the details. The product is cement—correct. The quantity is 1,000 tonnes—correct.\nMs. Chen: Good.\nFadi: But there is a small mistake. The correct reference number is PO-1243, not PO-1234.\nMs. Chen: Oh! You are right. Please correct it to PO-1243.\nFadi: Of course. Now the details are correct. I will confirm your order and send a confirmation email.\nMs. Chen: Thank you, Fadi. You are very careful.\n\nKarim: Fadi, please check the reference number on this order.\nFadi: OK. The PO says PO-1234. But our number is PO-1243.\nKarim: So it's wrong. What do you do now?\nFadi: First, I write to the customer. Then I ask them to correct it. After that, I confirm the order.\nKarim: Good. Don't confirm an order with a wrong number.\nFadi: Of course not. I always check first, then confirm.\nKarim: Perfect. That's the right way.","scene":"Meeting room"},"part-04-speaking":{"title":"Part 4 · Speaking and Your Role","intro":"Practise in pairs. Take turns and use the prompts as speaking cues.","exercises":[{"type":"checklist","prompt":"A. Role-play: Student A places and Student B checks the order. Then swap roles.","items":["A places an order: “I’d like to order…”","B asks for the PO: “Please send the purchase order.”","A gives the reference number.","B checks details: “First I read… Then I check…”","A corrects a detail. B confirms the order."]},{"type":"conversation","prompt":"B. Build the sample conversation: drag the speaker-labeled lines into the order that makes sense.","lines":[{"speaker":"Ms. Chen","text":"Hello, Fadi. I'd like to place an order. 1,000 tonnes of cement."},{"speaker":"Fadi","text":"Thank you, Ms. Chen. Please send me the purchase order."},{"speaker":"Ms. Chen","text":"I sent it this morning. The reference is PO-1234."},{"speaker":"Fadi","text":"Let me check. First, I read the PO. Then I check the details. The product is cement—correct. The quantity is 1,000 tonnes—correct."},{"speaker":"Ms. Chen","text":"Good."},{"speaker":"Fadi","text":"But there is a small mistake. The correct reference number is PO-1243, not PO-1234."},{"speaker":"Ms. Chen","text":"Oh! You are right. Please correct it to PO-1243."},{"speaker":"Fadi","text":"Of course. Now the details are correct. I will confirm your order and send a confirmation email."},{"speaker":"Ms. Chen","text":"Thank you, Fadi. You are very careful."}],"explain":"Ms. Chen places the order, Fadi asks for the PO and checks it, Ms. Chen corrects the reference, and Fadi promises the confirmation. Play the conversation above to hear each speaker."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"C. Tell your partner how to check an order. Use First…, Then…, and Don’t forget…","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"D. Discuss: Why is it important to check every detail? Why do we confirm an order in writing?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."}],"reading":"Ms. Chen: Hello, Fadi. I'd like to place an order. 1,000 tonnes of cement.\nFadi: Thank you, Ms. Chen. Please send me the purchase order.\nMs. Chen: I sent it this morning. The reference is PO-1234.\nFadi: Let me check. First, I read the PO. Then I check the details. The product is cement—correct. The quantity is 1,000 tonnes—correct.\nMs. Chen: Good.\nFadi: But there is a small mistake. The correct reference number is PO-1243, not PO-1234.\nMs. Chen: Oh! You are right. Please correct it to PO-1243.\nFadi: Of course. Now the details are correct. I will confirm your order and send a confirmation email.\nMs. Chen: Thank you, Fadi. You are very careful.","scene":"Customer service office"},"part-05-reading":{"title":"Part 5 · Extended Reading: The one wrong number","intro":"Read or listen to the complete passage. Pause to consider how one missing zero can affect a delivery.","exercises":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"What happens if someone writes 100 instead of 1,000 tonnes?","options":["The company sends too much","The customer receives one tenth of the order","The price doubles","Nothing changes"],"answer":"The customer receives one tenth of the order","explain":"100 tonnes is one tenth of 1,000 tonnes.","feedback":["Not quite: “The company sends too much” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The customer receives one tenth of the order”. 100 tonnes is one tenth of 1,000 tonnes.","Correct. 100 tonnes is one tenth of 1,000 tonnes.","Not quite: “The price doubles” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The customer receives one tenth of the order”. 100 tonnes is one tenth of 1,000 tonnes.","Not quite: “Nothing changes” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The customer receives one tenth of the order”. 100 tonnes is one tenth of 1,000 tonnes."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"What is the secret of checking well?","options":["Go fast","Check five things together","Go slowly and check one thing at a time","Wait until after delivery"],"answer":"Go slowly and check one thing at a time","explain":"The reading recommends a slow, one-detail-at-a-time check.","feedback":["Not quite: “Go fast” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Go slowly and check one thing at a time”. The reading recommends a slow, one-detail-at-a-time check.","Not quite: “Check five things together” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Go slowly and check one thing at a time”. The reading recommends a slow, one-detail-at-a-time check.","Correct. The reading recommends a slow, one-detail-at-a-time check.","Not quite: “Wait until after delivery” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Go slowly and check one thing at a time”. The reading recommends a slow, one-detail-at-a-time check."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"When you find a mistake, you should…","options":["ignore it","correct it","hide it","confirm anyway"],"answer":"correct it","explain":"The passage says to stop and correct even a tiny mistake.","feedback":["Not quite: “ignore it” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “correct it”. The passage says to stop and correct even a tiny mistake.","Correct. The passage says to stop and correct even a tiny mistake.","Not quite: “hide it” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “correct it”. The passage says to stop and correct even a tiny mistake.","Not quite: “confirm anyway” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “correct it”. The passage says to stop and correct even a tiny mistake."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"A written confirmation is like a…","options":["door","mirror","truck","price"],"answer":"mirror","explain":"It shows both sides all the order details.","feedback":["Not quite: “door” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “mirror”. It shows both sides all the order details.","Correct. It shows both sides all the order details.","Not quite: “truck” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “mirror”. It shows both sides all the order details.","Not quite: “price” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “mirror”. It shows both sides all the order details."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"One wrong number can become a ____ problem.","options":["small","big","funny","new"],"answer":"big","explain":"The reading explains that one missing zero can cause a very big problem.","feedback":["Not quite: “small” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “big”. The reading explains that one missing zero can cause a very big problem.","Correct. The reading explains that one missing zero can cause a very big problem.","Not quite: “funny” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “big”. The reading explains that one missing zero can cause a very big problem.","Not quite: “new” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “big”. The reading explains that one missing zero can cause a very big problem."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"A good checker is worth their weight in…","options":["cement","gold","iron","paper"],"answer":"gold","explain":"The passage uses the expression “worth their weight in gold.”","feedback":["Not quite: “cement” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “gold”. The passage uses the expression “worth their weight in gold.”","Correct. The passage uses the expression “worth their weight in gold.”","Not quite: “iron” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “gold”. The passage uses the expression “worth their weight in gold.”","Not quite: “paper” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “gold”. The passage uses the expression “worth their weight in gold.”"]},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"Complete the summary with one word.","items":[["A small ____ can become a big problem.","mistake"],["So ____ is very important.","checking"],["Go ____ and check one thing at a time.","slowly"],["When you find a mistake, ____ it.","correct"],["Always ____ in writing.","confirm"],["Both sides can see the ____.","details"]]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"True or false: You should check many things at once and do it fast.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explain":"The reading says not to rush or check five things at once.","feedback":["Not quite. The statement is false. The reading says not to rush or check five things at once.","Correct. The reading says not to rush or check five things at once."]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"Discuss: Have you seen a small mistake become a big problem? Why is written confirmation a good habit?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."}],"reading":"In business, small things are not small. A single wrong number in an order can become a very big problem. Imagine this. A customer orders 1,000 tonnes of cement. But someone writes “100” instead of “1,000”. Now the company sends 100 tonnes—one tenth of the order. The customer's building stops because there is not enough cement. The customer is angry. It all started with one missing zero.\n\nThis is why checking is so important. Checking is not exciting work. Nobody feels like a hero when they read an order carefully and find a small mistake. But that quiet, careful work saves the company from big problems. One person checks every detail: the product, quantity, price, address, and reference number. This is some of the most valuable work in the company. A good checker is worth their weight in gold.\n\nHow do you check well? Go slowly and check one thing at a time. First, the product: is it correct? Then the quantity: is the number right—and are all the zeros there? Next, the price. Then the customer's name and address. Then the reference number. Don't rush. Don't check five things at once. Check one thing, tick it, then the next. When you find a mistake—even a tiny one—don't ignore it. Stop and correct it. A small mistake, corrected now, is easy. The same mistake, found after delivery, is a disaster.\n\nThe best companies always confirm in writing. After you check the order, write a confirmation: “We confirm your order: cement, 1,000 tonnes, reference PO-1243.” Now both sides can see the details in writing. If there is a mistake, the customer sees it and says, “No, that's wrong.” The written confirmation is like a mirror—it shows both sides all the details. Check carefully, correct any mistake, and confirm in writing. Do these three simple things every time, and your orders will be right—and your partners will trust you.","scene":"Office"},"part-06-writing":{"title":"Part 6 · Writing: a real email","intro":"Study the model, arrange its parts, then write and review your own order-confirmation email.","exercises":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"What is the total in the model email?","options":["$4,500","$45,000","$450,000","$45 per tonne"],"answer":"$45,000","explain":"The email states 1,000 tonnes at $45 per tonne, for a total of $45,000.","feedback":["Not quite: “$4,500” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “$45,000”. The email states 1,000 tonnes at $45 per tonne, for a total of $45,000.","Correct. The email states 1,000 tonnes at $45 per tonne, for a total of $45,000.","Not quite: “$450,000” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “$45,000”. The email states 1,000 tonnes at $45 per tonne, for a total of $45,000.","Not quite: “$45 per tonne” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “$45,000”. The email states 1,000 tonnes at $45 per tonne, for a total of $45,000."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"What is the reference number?","options":["PO-1234","PO-1243","PO-4321","PO-1200"],"answer":"PO-1243","explain":"The corrected reference is PO-1243.","feedback":["Not quite: “PO-1234” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “PO-1243”. The corrected reference is PO-1243.","Correct. The corrected reference is PO-1243.","Not quite: “PO-4321” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “PO-1243”. The corrected reference is PO-1243.","Not quite: “PO-1200” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “PO-1243”. The corrected reference is PO-1243."]},{"type":"order","prompt":"B. Put the email parts in order.","items":["Dear Ms. Chen,","Thank you for your order.","We confirm: cement, 1,000 tonnes, total 45,000 dollars.","Reference: PO-1243. Your order is approved.","Best regards, Fadi."]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"C. Write a 40–60-word order-confirmation email. Include product, quantity, price, total, reference, and approval.","tip":"Checklist: greeting; thanks; product; quantity; unit price; total; reference; approval; sign-off. Save locally, copy, download, or print your draft."},{"type":"checklist","prompt":"D. Review your email.","items":["I said “Thank you for your order.”","I confirmed the product, quantity, and total.","I gave the reference number.","I said the order is approved."]}],"reading":"Subject: Order confirmation. Dear Ms. Chen, thank you for your order. We confirm: cement, 1,000 tonnes, 45 dollars per tonne, total 45,000 dollars. Reference: PO-1243. Your order is approved. We will send the delivery details soon. Best regards, Fadi.","scene":"Office"},"part-07-trade-skills":{"title":"Part 7 · Trade-Skills Track: Reading a purchase order","intro":"Inspect each field in a purchase order and check that the reply identifies the right order.","exercises":[{"type":"match","prompt":"D. Match the part of a PO with its example.","pairs":[["Reference no.","PO-1243"],["Customer","NorthBridge"],["Product","Cement"],["Quantity","1,000 tonnes"],["Total","$45,000"]]},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"B. Listen to Fadi read the PO and complete the missing word.","items":[["The reference ____ is PO-1243.","number"],["The ____ is NorthBridge.","customer"],["The product is cement, 1,000 ____.","tonnes"],["The ____ is 45,000 dollars.","total"]]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"What should you check against the quotation?","options":["Only the reference number","Product, quantity, and price","Only the customer name","The delivery driver"],"answer":"Product, quantity, and price","explain":"The reading specifically says these order details should match the quotation.","feedback":["Not quite: “Only the reference number” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Product, quantity, and price”. The reading specifically says these order details should match the quotation.","Correct. The reading specifically says these order details should match the quotation.","Not quite: “Only the customer name” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Product, quantity, and price”. The reading specifically says these order details should match the quotation.","Not quite: “The delivery driver” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Product, quantity, and price”. The reading specifically says these order details should match the quotation."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"A. What does a purchase order say?","options":["I want to buy","I have paid","The goods arrived","The account is closed"],"answer":"I want to buy","explain":"A PO is the document that says “I want to buy.”","feedback":["Correct. A PO is the document that says “I want to buy.”","Not quite: “I have paid” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “I want to buy”. A PO is the document that says “I want to buy.”","Not quite: “The goods arrived” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “I want to buy”. A PO is the document that says “I want to buy.”","Not quite: “The account is closed” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “I want to buy”. A PO is the document that says “I want to buy.”"]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Why is the reference number important?","options":["It names and separates the order","It gives the delivery address","It replaces the total","It confirms payment"],"answer":"It names and separates the order","explain":"The number keeps each order clear in a busy company.","feedback":["Correct. The number keeps each order clear in a busy company.","Not quite: “It gives the delivery address” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “It names and separates the order”. The number keeps each order clear in a busy company.","Not quite: “It replaces the total” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “It names and separates the order”. The number keeps each order clear in a busy company.","Not quite: “It confirms payment” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “It names and separates the order”. The number keeps each order clear in a busy company."]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"C. Look at an order (real or invented). Read it aloud, check each detail, and write a short confirmation with the reference number.","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"Practice: Why is it important to include the reference number in your reply?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."}],"reading":"The purchase order, or PO, is one of the most important documents in trade. It says “I want to buy.” When a PO arrives, your job is to read it, check it, and confirm it. A PO has clear parts, and you must check every one. The reference number names the order, like PO-1243. The customer is the company that buys. The product, quantity, and price are the order itself—check that they match the quotation. The total is the final number—check the maths. When you check a PO, use the reference number in your reply so both sides talk about the same order. This small habit stops confusion. In a busy company with many orders, the reference number keeps every order separate and clear.","scene":"Office"},"part-08-consolidation":{"title":"Part 8 · Consolidation: The careful checker","intro":"Follow Fadi’s check and catch the address mistake before the delivery is arranged.","exercises":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"How does Fadi check the order?","options":["Fast","Slowly, one detail at a time","Only the total","After delivery"],"answer":"Slowly, one detail at a time","explain":"The passage describes Fadi checking each order detail slowly.","feedback":["Not quite: “Fast” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Slowly, one detail at a time”. The passage describes Fadi checking each order detail slowly.","Correct. The passage describes Fadi checking each order detail slowly.","Not quite: “Only the total” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Slowly, one detail at a time”. The passage describes Fadi checking each order detail slowly.","Not quite: “After delivery” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Slowly, one detail at a time”. The passage describes Fadi checking each order detail slowly."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"What is wrong with the address?","options":["The city is wrong","Street 5 should be Street 15","The customer name is missing","The country is missing"],"answer":"Street 5 should be Street 15","explain":"The street number is missing the digit 1.","feedback":["Not quite: “The city is wrong” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Street 5 should be Street 15”. The street number is missing the digit 1.","Correct. The street number is missing the digit 1.","Not quite: “The customer name is missing” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Street 5 should be Street 15”. The street number is missing the digit 1.","Not quite: “The country is missing” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Street 5 should be Street 15”. The street number is missing the digit 1."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"What should Fadi do when he finds the problem?","options":["Send the order to Street 5","Ignore it","Ask the customer and correct it","Cancel all future orders"],"answer":"Ask the customer and correct it","explain":"He checks with the customer, then corrects the address.","feedback":["Not quite: “Send the order to Street 5” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Ask the customer and correct it”. He checks with the customer, then corrects the address.","Not quite: “Ignore it” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Ask the customer and correct it”. He checks with the customer, then corrects the address.","Correct. He checks with the customer, then corrects the address.","Not quite: “Cancel all future orders” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Ask the customer and correct it”. He checks with the customer, then corrects the address."]},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"Complete each sentence with one word.","items":[["Fadi checks the order ____, one detail at a time.","slowly"],["The street number is wrong—one missing ____.","1"],["A wrong ____ sends the delivery to the wrong place.","address"],["Fadi ____ the address and confirms the order.","corrects"],["Careful checks stop expensive ____.","mistakes"]]},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"D. Find words from the reading.","items":[["Where the goods must go → the ____.","address"],["Costing a lot of money → ____.","expensive"],["To keep safe from harm → to ____.","protect"]]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Fadi should confirm the order before asking about the address.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explain":"The mismatch must be clarified and corrected before confirmation.","feedback":["Not quite. The statement is false. The mismatch must be clarified and corrected before confirmation.","Correct. The mismatch must be clarified and corrected before confirmation."]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"Discuss: How did a small check save the company a big problem? Why is careful work valuable?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."}],"reading":"A new order arrives. It is a big one—5,000 tonnes of cement, for a new customer. Fadi is excited, but he does not hurry. He checks the order slowly, one detail at a time. First, the product: cement—correct. Then the quantity: 5,000 tonnes—correct. Then the price. Then the customer's name and address.\n\nThen Fadi checks the address again. Something is wrong. The city is right, but the street number is “Street 5,” and Fadi remembers the customer is on “Street 15.” One missing “1” could send the delivery to the wrong place. Fadi stops and writes to the customer: “Dear Sir, please can you check the delivery address? Is it Street 5 or Street 15?” The customer replies: “You are right—it is Street 15. Thank you for checking!”\n\nFadi corrects the address and confirms the order. Karim says: “Well done, Fadi. A wrong address on a 5,000-tonne order—that is a big, expensive mistake. You found it because you checked slowly and carefully. You are the person who protects every order.” Small, careful checks stop big, expensive mistakes.","scene":"Warehouse office"},"part-09-cases":{"title":"Part 9 · Case Studies and Decisions","intro":"Choose a careful action, explain why, and practise a polite clarification.","exercises":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"Case 1: The PO says 100 tonnes, but the customer asked for 1,000. What is the best action?","options":["Send 100 tonnes because that is on the PO","Stop and ask whether it should be 100 or 1,000","Send 1,000 without asking","Ignore the difference and confirm"],"answer":"Stop and ask whether it should be 100 or 1,000","explain":"Resolve the mismatch with the customer before confirming or shipping.","feedback":["Not quite: “Send 100 tonnes because that is on the PO” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Stop and ask whether it should be 100 or 1,000”. Resolve the mismatch with the customer before confirming or shipping.","Correct. Resolve the mismatch with the customer before confirming or shipping.","Not quite: “Send 1,000 without asking” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Stop and ask whether it should be 100 or 1,000”. Resolve the mismatch with the customer before confirming or shipping.","Not quite: “Ignore the difference and confirm” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Stop and ask whether it should be 100 or 1,000”. Resolve the mismatch with the customer before confirming or shipping."]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"Write one polite sentence to check the quantity with the customer.","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Case 2: A colleague confirms an order in ten seconds without checking. What did the colleague do wrong?","options":["Checked each detail carefully","Confirmed before checking the details","Used the reference number","Asked for clarification"],"answer":"Confirmed before checking the details","explain":"The price was later found to be wrong because the order was not checked.","feedback":["Not quite: “Checked each detail carefully” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Confirmed before checking the details”. The price was later found to be wrong because the order was not checked.","Correct. The price was later found to be wrong because the order was not checked.","Not quite: “Used the reference number” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Confirmed before checking the details”. The price was later found to be wrong because the order was not checked.","Not quite: “Asked for clarification” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Confirmed before checking the details”. The price was later found to be wrong because the order was not checked."]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"Case 2: What should the colleague do before confirming? Write one imperative about checking.","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"Case 3: Why is it a problem to forget the reference number when there are 50 orders this week?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"Write the first line of an email using reference number PO-1243.","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."}],"reading":null,"scene":"Office"},"part-10-review":{"title":"Part 10 · Review and Can-Do","intro":"Review unit vocabulary, grammar, listening, reading, and process steps.","exercises":[{"type":"blanks","prompt":"A. Vocabulary review.","items":[["A request to buy products is an ____.","order"],["The document a customer sends to buy is a ____ order.","purchase"],["To say “yes, we have your order” is to ____.","confirm"],["The number that names an order is the ____ number.","reference"],["The person or company who buys is the ____.","customer"]]},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"B. Grammar review.","items":[["Fadi ____ (check) the details.","checks"],["We ____ (confirm) every order.","confirm"],["____, we receive the order. (First / Finally)","First"],["____, we confirm it. (First / Finally)","Finally"],["____ the details, please. (instruction)","Check"],["____ forget the reference number.","Don’t"]]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"C. What do we receive first in the process?","options":["The invoice","The purchase order","The delivery note","The confirmation"],"answer":"The purchase order","explain":"The process begins by receiving the PO.","feedback":["Not quite: “The invoice” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The purchase order”. The process begins by receiving the PO.","Correct. The process begins by receiving the PO.","Not quite: “The delivery note” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The purchase order”. The process begins by receiving the PO.","Not quite: “The confirmation” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “The purchase order”. The process begins by receiving the PO."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence describes an action happening now?","options":["Fadi checks every order each day.","Fadi is checking this PO right now.","Fadi checked the PO yesterday.","Check the PO, please."],"answer":"Fadi is checking this PO right now.","explain":"'Right now' signals the present continuous: is + verb-ing. 'Each day' is a routine (present simple); 'yesterday' is past; 'Check' is an instruction.","feedback":["Not quite: “Fadi checks every order each day.” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Fadi is checking this PO right now.”. 'Right now' signals the present continuous: is + verb-ing. 'Each day' is a routine (present simple); 'yesterday' is past; 'Check' is an instruction.","Correct. 'Right now' signals the present continuous: is + verb-ing. 'Each day' is a routine (present simple); 'yesterday' is past; 'Check' is an instruction.","Not quite: “Fadi checked the PO yesterday.” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Fadi is checking this PO right now.”. 'Right now' signals the present continuous: is + verb-ing. 'Each day' is a routine (present simple); 'yesterday' is past; 'Check' is an instruction.","Not quite: “Check the PO, please.” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Fadi is checking this PO right now.”. 'Right now' signals the present continuous: is + verb-ing. 'Each day' is a routine (present simple); 'yesterday' is past; 'Check' is an instruction."]},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"C. Read the short process and answer.","items":[["What do we receive first?","purchase order"],["What do we do next?","check the details"],["What do we do finally?","confirm the order"]]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"D. In the listening confirmation, what is the reference number?","options":["PO-1234","PO-1243","PO-4321","PO-1200"],"answer":"PO-1243","explain":"The corrected order reference is PO-1243.","feedback":["Not quite: “PO-1234” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “PO-1243”. The corrected order reference is PO-1243.","Correct. The corrected order reference is PO-1243.","Not quite: “PO-4321” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “PO-1243”. The corrected order reference is PO-1243.","Not quite: “PO-1200” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “PO-1243”. The corrected order reference is PO-1243."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"D. What is the product and quantity in the listening?","options":["Cement, 1,000 tonnes","Iron, 100 tonnes","Cement, 500 tonnes","Steel, 1,000 tonnes"],"answer":"Cement, 1,000 tonnes","explain":"The teacher-read confirmation says cement, 1,000 tonnes.","feedback":["Correct. The teacher-read confirmation says cement, 1,000 tonnes.","Not quite: “Iron, 100 tonnes” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Cement, 1,000 tonnes”. The teacher-read confirmation says cement, 1,000 tonnes.","Not quite: “Cement, 500 tonnes” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Cement, 1,000 tonnes”. The teacher-read confirmation says cement, 1,000 tonnes.","Not quite: “Steel, 1,000 tonnes” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Cement, 1,000 tonnes”. The teacher-read confirmation says cement, 1,000 tonnes."]},{"type":"choice","prompt":"D. Is the order approved?","options":["Yes","No","The speaker does not say"],"answer":"Yes","explain":"The confirmation says, “Your order is approved.”","feedback":["Correct. The confirmation says, “Your order is approved.”","Not quite: “No” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Yes”. The confirmation says, “Your order is approved.”","Not quite: “The speaker does not say” does not fit this clue. The best answer is “Yes”. The confirmation says, “Your order is approved.”"]},{"type":"checklist","prompt":"E. Speaking: practise with a partner. One person places an order; the other checks details and confirms.","items":["I placed an order.","I checked the details.","I corrected a mismatch.","I confirmed clearly."]},{"type":"writing","prompt":"F. Write two instructions: one positive and one negative (Don’t…).","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"blanks","prompt":"G. Error correction.","items":[["Fadi ____ the order. (check)","checks"],["You ____ the details. (checks)","check"],["____ the order, please. (To confirm)","Confirm"],["____ forget the number. (Not)","Don’t"],["The system ____ a reply. (send)","sends"]]},{"type":"match","prompt":"H. Match the step to the sequence word.","pairs":[["receive the order","First"],["check the details","Then"],["correct the mistake","Next"],["prepare the confirmation","After that"],["confirm the order","Finally"]]},{"type":"match","prompt":"I. Match each document to its job.","pairs":[["purchase order","the customer buys"],["confirmation","we say “yes”"],["invoice","the bill for money"],["delivery note","comes with the goods"],["reference number","names the order"]]},{"type":"checklist","prompt":"Can-Do check: rate your confidence and tick what you can do.","items":["I can receive and confirm an order.","I can check and correct the details.","I can give simple instructions (first, then…).","I can write an order-confirmation email."]}],"reading":"First, we receive the purchase order. Then we check the details—the product, quantity, price, and reference number. Next, we correct any mistake. Finally, we confirm the order and send a confirmation email. Every order, the same way.","scene":"Office"},"part-11-foundations":{"title":"Part 11 · Foundations for Further Study: The quiet power of care","intro":"Listen, reflect, and connect the unit’s checking habits to your own work.","exercises":[{"type":"writing","prompt":"A. What quiet quality is this unit really about?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"What is the difference between the fast-but-careless worker and the careful worker?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"Why is careful faster than careless in the end?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"Besides correct work, what does care build?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"B. With a partner, describe a time a small mistake caused a big problem. How could a careful check stop it?","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."},{"type":"writing","prompt":"C. Optional micro-writing: write 30–50 words about the steps of a job you do. Use First…, Then…, Next…, Finally… and at least one imperative.","tip":"Use the checklist in the feedback panel to review your answer."}],"reading":"This unit is about orders and documents. But hidden inside it is one of the most important qualities in all work: care. Care is the quiet habit of doing small things properly. It is not exciting, but it is valuable.\n\nThink about two kinds of workers. The first is fast but careless. They finish quickly, but they make small mistakes—a wrong number or a missing detail. Their work creates problems for everyone else, and the problems cost time and money to fix. The second worker is careful. They go a little slower, check their work, catch mistakes, and produce correct work. Who is really faster? The careful one, because nobody has to do the work twice.\n\nCareful is faster than careless in the end. A mistake caught now takes one minute to fix. Found later, it can take days and cost a lot. Careful workers save time and money and build trust. When people know your work is correct, they give you bigger, more important jobs. Care is how a junior becomes a manager.\n\nWhatever your job, bring care to it. Check your work before you send it. Read the number twice. Correct a small mistake now, not later. Do the quiet, careful thing every time. It will make you someone people trust.","scene":"Office"}}};
